# Line endings are part of the bytes, and this repo hashes bytes.
#
# Two things depend on a file having the SAME contents everywhere: the `?v=`
# script versions (scripts/stamp-assets.mjs) and the CSP inline-script hashes
# (scripts/csp.mjs). A browser hashes exactly what was served; if a Windows
# checkout produced CRLF while CI computed LF, the versions would disagree and
# the enforced CSP would block the page's own boot script.
#
# Today's tree is LF only by luck — the files were written that way and git
# hasn't re-checked them out. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules here, a
# fresh clone on Windows would convert them and both hashes would break, on
# someone else's machine, for reasons that look like nonsense.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
